{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795050615,"nonce":"VOJ+uCUotAfYdgja4lYt2VCxqs0=","title":"LocaleChain picks up a HA language change without a reload","message":"From the spec-axis review of the localisation effort (spec 11052b1, §locale-chain / Story 2): LocaleChain fetches /api/locale once at page load. If HA is unreachable at that moment the chain silently falls back to the browser locale; when the backend later reconnects and refresh_config republishes a language, the frontend never re-fetches, so the app stays on the browser locale until a manual reload.\n\nDesired: the frontend notices a backend language change without a reload (refetch on the live channel's reconnect signal, or a tracked resource the app already refreshes), keeping the chain HA → navigator → en.\n\nBackend half is already correct (refresh on every reconnect, tests/ha.rs).","files":null}]}